  "description": "The Blue Pig is ideal for all-mountain riding, enduro racing, technical singletrack and long-days in the saddle. This frame provides stable, reliable and agile performance suited to descending or climbing anywhere on the mountainside. And, it's Chromoly (CrMo) construction is engineered to be robust, lightweight and supple for the greatest comfort, reliability and control.\nIf you have heard of Ragley, you already know the Blue Pig name. From the early days of the ‘hardcore hardtail’ it has pushed the geometry envelope and been loved by anyone who rides for all-out grin-inducing fun.\nThe 2021 Blue Pig keeps the flame burning strong: Custom triple butted 4130 Chromoly tubing, ISCG 05 tabs, a 44mm head tube, internal dropper routing and a 148x12mm boost rear end. But it’s the geometry that defines it: the 63.75 degree head angle making its rowdy intentions abundantly clear.\nComfortable enough to ride all-day, tough enough for the bike park and flighty enough to speederbike through the local woodland loam. The Blue Pig is built to take abuse and inspire confidence when things get gnarly, but it’s not been pillaging the trough; it’s light to ride and quite happy putting in the miles to get to the good stuff.\nIf you don’t think a hardtail is capable, you’ve been riding the wrong bike…",
